    "updated_at": "2024-10-04T05:44:15Z",
    "body": "I actually wonder if this might be something we could simply fix. Code that follows the pattern in my first comment won't break, it will simply take the records before `disconnect()` is called. And the rest is already broken — I'd wager it's highly unlikely that code depends on pending records _not_ being taken.\r\n\r\nIf not, another solution is to introduce a _different_ method, and deprecate `disconnect()`. Though this is a conventional name at this point that other observers share too…\r\n\r\n@annevk What do you think?",
